Known non-deterministic corruption in the ARM64 build of z3-4.3.1 in
OpenJML/Solvers: the response to one of this test's commands contains
spurious "unexpected character" errors whose exact text (column ranges,
count) differs from run to run against the identical binary -- confirmed
by comparing two separate CI captures. A .bad golden (exact-match) can
never stay in sync with genuinely non-deterministic output, so this is
skipped rather than pinned to one observed variant. Never seen on x64.
See the jsmtlib_ci_cross_platform_verification memory for the broader
ARM64 z3-4.3.1 correctness-bug writeup (also includes confirmed sat/unsat
flips on other tests, which ARE deterministic and remain .bad goldens).
